; A sequence break deferred while the scheduler runs is the machine's, not the
; scheduler stack group's (sys/ucadr/uc-stack-groups.lisp, sgent; QUUX's
; Ethernet contract, section 2.6; lisp/sb-deferral.lisp).  Each trial defers
; a clock break in the scheduler's pass and times the next pass: a pass or two
; with the flag the machine's (6-13 ms on micro at 19 ns), about a second with
; MIT's sgent, which dropped the break when the scheduler resumed a compute
; process.  The bound is 100 ms, six ticks.  Run at the clock's default rate,
; 60 ticks.

; the bit's position and size, from qcom's m-flags fields: <18>
(list (lsh si:%%m-flags-deferred-sequence-break -6) (logand si:%%m-flags-deferred-sequence-break 63)) => (18 1)
; three trials, each gap under 100 ms
(sbd-trials 3) => (T T T)
; their gaps in microseconds, for the record
sbd-gaps
; a coroutine called inside a without-interrupts after a break was deferred
; there: the callee takes it, so the caller's bit after the return is 0 (mit's
; sgent gave back the caller's 1)
(second (sbd-coroutine)) => 0
(sbd-coroutine)
